You will be brought before governors and kings because of me. You will be witnesses for them and for those who are not Jews.
But when they arrest you, don't worry about what you will say or how you will say it. At that time you will be given the right words to say. However, when they arrest you, do not worry about what you will say or how you will say it. At that moment, you will be given the words you should speak.
It is not you who will speak, but the Spirit of your Father will speak through you.
Brothers will deliver their brothers to be killed. Fathers will deliver their children. Children will rise up against their parents and kill them.
Everyone will hate you because of me. But the one who endures to the end will be saved.
When people attack you in one place, flee to another. What I will tell you is true. You will not finish going through the cities of Israel before the Son of Man comes.
A student is no better than his teacher. A servant is no better than his master.
It is sufficient for a student to be like his teacher, and it is sufficient for a servant to be like his master. If the head of the household is called Baal Zebul, what can others who live there expect?
Do not fear your enemies. Whatever is secret will be revealed, and whatever is hidden will be brought to light.
What I tell you in the dark, speak in the light. What is whispered in your ear, proclaim from the rooftops.
Do not fear those who kill the body and cannot kill the soul; rather, fear the One who is able to destroy both body and soul in hell.
Do not two sparrows sell for a farthing? Yet one of them shall not fall on the ground without your Father.
