Jesus is the Lord of the Sabbath.
On the Sabbath, Jesus was walking in the fields, and his disciples were hungry, so they began to pluck ears of grain and eat.
The Pharisees saw this. They said to Jesus, "Look! It is not lawful to do this on the Sabbath. But your disciples are doing it anyway!"
Jesus answered, "Haven't you read what David did? He and his men were hungry.
He entered the house of God. He and his men ate the holy bread. Only the priests were allowed to eat it.
Haven't you read the law? It shows how the priests in the temple must work on the Sabbath day. But they are not considered guilty.
I tell you that which is greater than the temple is here.
The holy books say: "I desire mercy and not sacrifice." (Ezekiel 6:6) You do not know what these words mean. If you knew, you would not accuse those who are innocent.
The Son of Man is Lord of the Sabbath.
Leaving that place, Jesus entered their synagogue.
