He said to them, "Why is it that none of you, if his sheep falls into a pit on the Sabbath, will lift it out?"
A human being is of more value than sheep! Therefore, the law is permitting us to do good on the Sabbath.
Then Jesus said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." So he stretched it out. It was as good as new, just as good as the other hand.
But the Pharisees went out and plotted to kill Jesus, God's chosen servant.
Jesus knew all the plans the Pharisees had, so he left that place. Many people followed him, and he healed all their sick.
But he warned them not to tell who it was.
