The kingdom of heaven is like a treasure hidden in a field. When he found it, he went and sold all that he had and bought that field.
Again, the Kingdom of Heaven is like a merchant who was looking for a fine pearl.
He found one that was of great value. So he went and sold everything he owned. And he bought that pearl. The Parable of the Net.
Again, the kingdom of heaven is like a net. It was cast into the sea. And it gathered every kind of fish.
When it was full, the fishermen pulled it up on the shore. Then they sat down and gathered the good fish into baskets. But they threw the bad fish away.
This is what the Day of Judgment will be like. The angels will come. They will separate those who did what is wrong from those who did what is right.
The wicked will be cast into the burning oven. There the wicked will weep and gnash their teeth.
