John was telling Herod, "You have no right to marry her, it is against the law."
Herod wanted to kill John, but he was afraid of the people, because they believed that John was a prophet.
On Herod's birthday, Herodias's daughter danced for Herod and his guests. He was so pleased with her dancing.
He swore to her that he would give her anything she asked for.
Her mother told her what to say. So I told Herod, "Give me the head of John the Baptist on a large plate." I told her what to say.
The king was very angry. But he thought of his promise and the dinner guests. So he ordered one of his men to give her what she asked for.
