After he sent them, he went up to a mountain by himself to pray. When evening came, he was there alone.
The ship had long since distanced itself from the shore. It was crashing against the waves because the wind was blowing against it.
Early in the morning, Jesus went out to the disciples. He walked on the surface of the lake.
They saw him walking on the lake, so they were afraid. "He is a ghost!" they said. And they cried from fear.
Immediately Jesus spoke to them, saying, "Be of good cheer! I am He; do not be afraid."
