They came together in Galilee. Then Jesus said to them, "The Son of Man will be delivered into the hands of men."
They will kill him, and on the third day he will rise from the dead." Then the disciples were filled with deep sorrow. Jesus is being led to pay the temple tax.
Jesus and his disciples came to Capernaum. There a crowd came to Peter. They said to him, "Does not your teacher pay the temple tax?"
"Yes, he does that," he answered. When Peter entered the house, Jesus spoke first. "What do you think, Simon?" he asked. "Who among men, when they gather the taxes of the kings of the earth, do they gather from their own sons or from others?"
"From others," Peter answered. "For children are not to pay," Jesus told him.
But we do not want to anger them. Go to the lake and cast your hook. Take the first fish you catch. Open its mouth. There you will find the exact coin you need. Take it and give it to them as a tribute for you and me.
